	(text_box "CH32V006, picked for cost. Every pin is used up, even RST pin!\n\n- TIM1: center-aligned PWM on DRV_IN1/IN2. CCR4 is the ADC phase knob.\n- OPA runs in bare mode with an external 4R diff network. PD4 is the feedback node, and the ADC reads the amp on internal channel IN9.\n- USART1 HDSEL = osc-native bus. One wire, no TX_EN.\n- USART2 HDSEL = TEL, 20 kHz raw kernel telemetry over DMA ch6.\n- I2C1 = expansion/Qwiic, polled (DMA ch6/7 are taken).\n\nJP3 BOOTSTRAP: PD7 comes from the factory as RST (RST_MODE=10). Ship with the jumper open. First boot is a one-time bootstrap: flash, use the probe to set User Option Bytes RST_MODE=11 so PD7 becomes a GPIO,\nthen close the jumper with solder. Don't close it early! On an unprovisioned chip the OPA network parks the pin near GND and the chip is held in reset. Recovery = reopen the jumper.\n\nV006 has no CMP units, so protection is layered instead. DRV OCP/TSD catches shorts. Kernel I2t forces DRV_EN low + a latched STALL_FAULT that only the user can clear (firmware never re-enables itself). IWDG covers hung firmware, and any reset kills the bridge via the DRV_EN pulldown. TEL/DATA LEDs are just passive activity lamps. STAT is the only firmware-driven one (active low)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 172.72 29.21 0)
		(size 109.22 100.9649)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "420d38a1-53bd-4343-97a5-b28333868320")
	)
